<br/>
<i>If you are in a group with haste buffs you can reforge haste slightly more aggressively and gain more crit.</i>
<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="where-to-get-gear">Where to get gear</h5>You have a few key sources of gear before you go into raid. Dungeons will be your primary source but you'd like to get into Elemental Rune dungeons as soon as possible so if you have the resources it can be useful to supplement early gear with Bind on Equip items including the blue PVP set. The secondaries aren't optimal but getting high item level gear as soon as possible is your priority. You'll also get <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> and <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> from dungeons which let you buy higher item level gear. If you played this character in previous phases you might also have access to areas like the Molten Front, Archaeology or some professions.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="new-in-phase-4">New in Phase 4</h5>Phase 4 introduces a new form of dungeon content: <b>Elemental Rune: Protocol Twilight</b> which offers a large range of quite high item level pieces. Once you're able to complete these, you'll use them for most of your pre-Dragon Soul gearing. They drop lower item level versions of Dragon Soul Gear, along with some gear that drops in the Firelands raid. You will want to move to this content as soon as possible.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="priority-stats">Priority Stats</h5>We'll be looking for these stats on our Pre-BiS pieces, and as always we'll seek out our highest item level pieces when possible:<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Intellect:</b> Our most important stat. Always a priority.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Spirit</b>: Spirit is particularly valuable when undergeared since sustaining your mana through even a short fight can be stressful.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Haste Rating:</b> You need to aim for 12.52% Haste while buffed. After that, haste isn't a priority anymore.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Mastery:</b> Near identical in value to Crit. It doesn't matter too much which of the two you get on gear.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Critical Strike</b>: Similar in value to Mastery.</div></li></ol>You will want to socket <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52207/brilliant-inferno-ruby">
<img alt="Brilliant Inferno Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cutgemsuperior6.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brilliant Inferno Ruby</span></a> gems in the majority of your sockets regardless of color, unless the socket is better than the overall gain from <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52207/brilliant-inferno-ruby">
<img alt="Brilliant Inferno Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cutgemsuperior6.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brilliant Inferno Ruby</span></a>. Bear in mind that <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52296/ember-shadowspirit-diamond">
<img alt="Ember Shadowspirit Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_metagem_b.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ember Shadowspirit Diamond</span></a> requires 2 yellow gems to activate, so you will need to socket a minimum of two <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52208/reckless-ember-topaz">
<img alt="Reckless Ember Topaz" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cutgemsuperior4.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reckless Ember Topaz</span></a>. Outside of that, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52236/purified-demonseye">
<img alt="Purified Demonseye" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cutgemsuperior3.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Purified Demonseye</span></a> are a great gem for Holy Priests.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="cataclysm-currencies">Cataclysm Currencies</h2>
<div class="clear"></div>
<div class="tabs-wrapper">
<div id="dsf67g4d-currencies">
<div class="tabs-container">
<ul class="tabs" role="tablist">
<li data-first-in-row="true" data-selected="true" role="tab">
<a href="#currencies-justice-points" rel="np" tabindex="-1">
<div>
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/small/pvecurrency-justice.jpg");'></span>Justice Points</div>
<b>
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif");'></span>Justice Points</b></a></li>
<li data-first-in-row="false" role="tab">
<a href="#currencies-valor-points" rel="np">
<div>
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/small/pvecurrency-valor.jpg");'></span>Valor Points</div>
<b>
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif");'></span>Valor Points</b></a></li>
<li data-first-in-row="false" role="tab">
<a href="#currencies-obsidian-fragments" rel="np">
<div>
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/small/inv_stone_15.jpg");'></span>Obsidian Fragments</div>
<b>
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif");'></span>Obsidian Fragments</b></a></li>
<div class="vertical-scroll-shadow"></div>
<div class="horizontal-scroll-shadow"></div></ul></div></div>
<div class="tabbed-contents">
<div id="tab-currencies-justice-points" style="">
<h3 class="heading-size-3 first" id="justice-points-for-holy-priest-healer-pre-raid">Justice Points for Holy Priest Healer Pre-Raid</h3>
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> are the Cataclysm version of <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=101/emblem-of-heroism">
<span>
<img alt="Emblem of Heroism" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_proclaimchampion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Heroism</span></span></a>, and they can be obtained by killing bosses in Heroic Dungeons and completing Random Dungeons through the Random Dungeon Finder tool. The main vendors you can exchange these at to obtain gear are <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=46555/gunra">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Gunra</span></a> for the Horde and <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=44246/magatha-silverton">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Magatha Silverton</span></a> for the Alliance.<br/>
<br/>With Phase 4, Phase 2 items that previously cost <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> are now purchasable using <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a>. These are all catch up or starter pieces now so you don't have to worry as much about what order you buy them in. You'll eventually replace every slot with either Valor or Obsidian Fragment items so none of these are permanent. I'd recommend you prioritize the 378 items - particularly <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71211/soothing-brimstone-circle">
<img alt="Soothing Brimstone Circle" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_firelandsraid_02c.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soothing Brimstone Circle</span></a> since it's well itemized and will let you spend your more premium currencies on other slots but there are no wrong answers in regards to what you buy.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="wh-center" style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
