<div id="tab-currencies-obsidian-fragments" style="display: none;">
<h3 class="heading-size-3 first" id="obsidian-fragments-for-holy-priest-healer-pre-raid">Obsidian Fragments for Holy Priest Healer Pre-Raid</h3>
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3281/obsidian-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Obsidian Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Fragment</span></span></a> is a new currency introduced in the fourth phase of Cataclysm Classic, which you can obtain through <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/guide/dungeons/protocol-twilight-dungeons-overview">Elemental Rune Protocol Twilight Dungeons</a>. Similar currencies were available in previous phases. There are items you can buy in every single slot and most of your pre-raid gearing will take place here. I'll list a few particularly good pieces that you'll want to get first, but after you obtain those you can mostly just upgrade your weakest slots.<br/>
<br/>It's first on the list, but I'll stress just how powerful <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78485/maw-of-the-dragonlord">
<img alt="Maw of the Dragonlord" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_1h_deathwingraiddw_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Maw of the Dragonlord</span></a> is. However, most items on this list are also possible drops from the dungeons themselves. PTR testing revealed that <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78485/maw-of-the-dragonlord">
<img alt="Maw of the Dragonlord" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_1h_deathwingraiddw_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Maw of the Dragonlord</span></a> was mostly likely to drop from Vortex Pinnacle so where possible try and farm that since it might save you 75 <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3281/obsidian-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Obsidian Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Fragment</span></span></a>. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77976/heart-of-unliving">
<img alt="Heart of Unliving" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_qirajicrystal_05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart of Unliving</span></a> is also very powerful.<br/>
<br/>You can also buy lower item level versions of your T13 tier set. If you already have a T12 four set then these are lower priority. If you don't, then you can pick up your T13 set after the two more powerful options in the previous paragraph.<br/>
<br/>
